-- title:
--   Retained symbol factorizations give a slow-rational-lower-degree factorization of the orbit
-- statement:
--   For every natural number $s$ there is a natural number $C \ge 2$ with the following property. Let $\sigma$, $J$ be finite types, $L$ a Lie algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, $d \in \mathbb{N}$, and give $\mathbb{R} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ a Hausdorff topology making it a topological additive group with continuous real scalar multiplication. Let $D$ be a `RationalFilteredNilmanifold L (s+1) d` (OpenAI's structure bundling a nilpotent filtration of $L$ of length $s+1$, a $\mathbb{Q}$-basis of $L$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\ d$, layer bases, a lattice and a grid), and $w : \mathrm{Fin}\ d \to \mathbb{N}$ weights such that every layer $j$ of the filtration is the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of the basis vectors $i$ with $j \le w_i$ (hypothesis $hF$). Write $\mathfrak{g}$ for the associated graded algebra `D.filtration.AssociatedGraded`, $\beta$ for its basis `D.filtration.associatedGradedBasis D.basis w hF`, and `rationalLogHeight q` $= \log\max(|\mathrm{num}\,q|, \mathrm{den}\,q)$. Let $U : J \to$ (Lie subalgebras of $\mathfrak{g}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$), $v : J \to (\mathrm{Fin}\ d \to \mathfrak{g})$, $n, \mathrm{aux}, \mathrm{oldModulus} : J \to \mathbb{N}$, $M \in \mathbb{N}$ and $p \in \mathbb{R}$. Assume: $0 \le p$; `D.GeometryComplexityLE p` (OpenAI's bound: $d \le p$, $\mathrm{grid} \le e^p$, and log-heights of structure constants and layer-basis coordinates at most $p$); $|\sigma| \le p$ and $|J| \le p$; for each $j$, the span of the range of $v_j$ is $U_j$, $U_j$ is `BasisGradedSubmodule β w` (closed under the grade projections of $\beta$), and every $\beta$-coordinate of every $v_j(i)$ has log-height at most $p$; $n_j, \mathrm{aux}_j, \mathrm{oldModulus}_j > 0$ for all $j$ and $M > 0$; $\mathrm{oldModulus}_j \mid M$; $n_j \le e^p$ and $\mathrm{aux}_j \le e^p$. Then for all $W, A : \sigma \to \mathbb{R}$ with $\exp((p+C)^C) \le A_i$ for all $i$, every niltest $T$ : `D.Niltest (fun _ : σ => 1)`, and all $\mathrm{shift} : \sigma \to \mathbb{Q}$, $\mathrm{oldShift} : J \to \sigma \to \mathbb{Q}$, $\mathrm{oldSides} : J \to \sigma \to \mathbb{R}$, if $\mathrm{oldSides}_{j,i} > 0$, $M A_i \le W_i$, $e^{-p} W_i \le \mathrm{oldModulus}_j\,\mathrm{aux}_j\,\mathrm{oldSides}_{j,i}$ for all $j, i$, and for each $j$ the symbol of `T.scalarAffinePullback (oldModulus j * aux j) (oldShift j)` (the niltest with orbit precomposed by $x \mapsto r x + \mathrm{shift}$) satisfies `D.filtration.SymbolFactorizationIn D.basis w hF (oldSides j) _ p (n j) (U j)` (OpenAI's predicate: the symbol factors as $E \cdot P \cdot R$ with $E$ slow at scales $\mathrm{oldSides}_j$ with bound $e^p$, $R$ on the rational grid of level $n_j$, and $P$ with coefficients in the realification of the pointwise subalgebra generated by $U_j$), then, writing $\mathrm{current} = $ `T.scalarAffinePullback M shift` and $g$ for its orbit's logarithm viewed as an element of the group of the adapted polynomial filtration `D.filtration.realification.adaptedPolynomialFiltration (fun _ => 1)`, there exist $v_0 : \mathrm{Fin}\ d \to \mathfrak{g}$, $m \in \mathbb{N}$, $\kappa \in$ `D.RealGroup`, and $E, b, R$ in that group, such that, with $U_\infty = \bigcap_j U_j$:
--   the span of the range of $v_0$ is $U_\infty$; $U_\infty$ is `BasisGradedSubmodule β w`; every $\beta$-coordinate of every $v_0(i)$ has log-height at most $(p+C)^C$; $0 < m \le \exp((p+C)^C)$ and $n_j\,\mathrm{aux}_j^{s+1} \mid m$ for all $j$; $\kappa$ lies in `D.realLattice`; $E \cdot b \cdot R \cdot \iota(\kappa) = g$, where $\iota$ is `adaptedConstantGroupHom (fun _ => 1)`; for every monomial exponent $\alpha$ and index $i$, the $i$-th coordinate (in the real base change of $D$'s basis) of the $\alpha$-coefficient of $E$'s vector polynomial is at most $\exp((p+C)^C)/\prod_i A_i^{\alpha_i}$ in absolute value (`monomialScale A α`); the family of all coordinates of the coefficients of $R$ lies in `realDenominatorGrid m` (vectors $x$ with $m x$ integral); the constant coefficients of $b$ and $R$ are $0$; every $\alpha$-coefficient of $b$ lies in `D.filtration.realGradedRefiltrationLayer U∞ |α|`; for every $t \in \mathbb{R}^\sigma$, the evaluation of $b$ at $t$ lies in the realification of `D.filtration.gradedRefiltrationSubalgebra U∞`; and `D.filtration.HasNativeLowerDegreeOrbit U∞ (fun _ => 1) b` holds (OpenAI's predicate: $b$ comes from a polynomial orbit of the graded refiltration by $U_\infty$ with zero constant term whose image in the top quotient has degree at most $s$).
